{"completed": true, "response": "<escape>{\n  \"report_supported\": \"partly\",\n  \"judge_supported\": \"partly\",\n  \"report_quotes\": [\n    \"According to the entropy hypothesis, the increased entropy demonstrated in Freezers compared to non-freezers during normal stepping and in Freezers themselves during periods of FOG may suggest greater errors in subthalamic outflow sensorimotor information processing in Freezers and motor inhibition, which may be reflected in abnormal gait patterns when not freezing, and during FOG.\",\n    \"In contrast to the entropy hypothesis outlined above, an alternate hypothesis has been proposed: high beta power and low beta entropy represent lower information transfer capacity in sensorimotor cortical rhythms and in the STN LFP at the onset and offset of movement...\",\n    \"This alternative hypothesis would suggest that the low beta power and high beta entropy seen in the current study would lead to higher information transfer in sensorimotor rhythms that may reflect a compensatory attempt to overcome the abnormal gait in Freezers.\",\n    \"These results support the current neuronal entropy hypothesis and suggest that greater unpredictability in the STN beta rhythm may contribute to more asymmetric and arrhythmic gait and greater unpredictability in alpha rhythms may contribute to FOG. Conversely increased entropy in alpha/beta rhythms may be a compensatory attempt to improve the gait impairment.\"\n  ],\n  \"judge_quotes\": [\n    \"The predictability of the LFPs (band-pass filtered between 8–12 Hz for alpha and 13–30 Hz for beta) was analyzed using Sample Entropy 11 (SampEn), a nonlinear measure suitable for physiological time series.\",\n    \"Freezers also showed increased alpha SampEn during FOG when compared to walking without FOG (F(1, 51) = 7.67, P = 0.005).\",\n    \"Nonlinear signal analysis demonstrated that SampEn in the beta band was greater during SIP (without FOG) in Freezers compared to Non-Freezers (H(1) = 4.61, P = 0.032).\",\n    \"FOG in the FW and TBC tasks were identified in the video recordings by a neurologist as a change from the subject’s forward walking pattern that included shortened, faster steps (festination) and periods of no forward motion.\"\n  ],\n  \"why\": \"报告的说法部分有依据。2017年论文确实明确提出了两种相竞争的机制解释：一种认为较高的神经熵反映信息处理错误和运动抑制，具有病理意义；另一种认为较高的beta熵可能提高感觉运动信息传递，是克服步态障碍的代偿机制。论文甚至明确使用“In contrast”和“alternate hypothesis”描述两者，并在结论中指出熵增加可能具有病理作用，也可能具有代偿作用。因此，不能认为报告凭空建立了病理性与代偿性的竞争解释。但是，论文并未提出H11与H12具有相反的时间顺序预测，也没有把所有熵及复杂度指标认定为同一个神经现象。尤其需要区分两项实际结果：beta SampEn是在无FOG的原地踏步（SIP）期间比较Freezers与Non-Freezers；alpha SampEn则是在Freezers内部比较FOG期间与无FOG步行期间。论文的替代假说主要针对低beta功率和高beta熵，并引用了既往beta复杂度研究，不能据此推导出所有不同指标、频段和行为阶段都是同一现象的相反预测。因此，报告的总体机制解释有依据，但其时间顺序和现象同一性的表述缺少全文支持。指控者的说法也部分有依据：其对2017年研究的alpha频段发现描述准确，论文明确报告了FOG期间alpha SampEn高于无冻结步行期间。不过，这不是2017年论文唯一的熵结果，论文还报告了无FOG原地踏步期间Freezers的beta SampEn高于Non-Freezers。指控者关于2026年预印本的Shannon entropy、Lempel-Ziv complexity、beta burst timing及比较基线的描述，均无法从本附件的2017年全文核实；同样，两个研究之间的算法、频段和时间阶段是否确实不同，也不能仅凭这篇论文完整确认。故不能把指控者的整体说法评为全文明确支持，也不能认定其与全文矛盾。\"\n}</escape>", "metadata": {"session_handle": "0e54ae73-34e7-42bb-81da-cd6b7fd5e1c9", "session_revision": 0, "session_ttl_max_hours": 6, "job_directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt3\\pro-bridge-20261114T073844166759Z", "elapsed_seconds": 169.5, "completed_utc": "2026-11-14T07:41:33.669154+00:00", "model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "temporary": true, "unpersonalized": true, "generation_policy_verified": true, "request_policy": {"model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "history_and_training_disabled": true, "temporary_chat_requests_personalization": false, "is_do_not_remember": false, "continuation": false, "unpersonalized_inherited_verified": false, "body_sha256": "7c598e92f30a350c9ea55d164c63a9b874d089b882301351a5778f2687680d2a", "attachment_count": 1}, "stream_completion": {"sse_done": true, "message_completed": true, "independent_terminal_verified": true}, "profile": "yi/local-codex-auth", "account_sha256": "b3efb6361563c139233ed7b7ef61a7c9afe0bd48d4eb3525dbe31956b024d6da", "transport": "probridge-pure-http", "resume_requests": 0, "topic_connections": 0, "browser_started": false, "Docker_used": false, "automatic_retry": false, "initializer_pss_limit_mib": "not_applicable_no_browser", "attachment_count": 1, "code_sha256": {"tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_cli.py": "96a4cdb6cd5d982f4d1de5b6ba8fae0cf23ee44aa3e41d7fdf6968e3fb590e48", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_sessions.py": "83a3ed4ae1efa9f1a2b8ee3f144cc0dc9f668f995a33cc4222308cb3fa31f683", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_attachments.py": "eedfa23885000025700f6306b1d1f4582896a7370734be506c156dee532fd7d7"}}, "screenshot_evidence": {"complete": true, "kind": "offline_actual_HTTP_response", "directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt3\\pro-bridge-20261114T073844166759Z", "files": ["proof-offline.png"], "sha256": {"proof-offline.png": "f2687daf9ac1f484ea38231ebc9b722d82a404d83ce457443f3795b0183e6174"}}}
